WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:17.270
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.940
to air in 2022.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.840
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.360
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.960
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.050
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:45.370
That's Fire And Blood volume 1. The yet unreleased
Fire And Blood volume 2 will continue from

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:51.670
where part 1 ended, with Rhaenyra Targaryen's
son Aegon lll's reign and will cover Blackyre

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:56.400
rebellions, the war with Dorne and go all
the way to the Mad King and Robert's Rebellion

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.520
that ended Targaryen dynasty.
The key event of the prequel will be the Dance

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:05.670
of the Dragon, a Targaryen civil war.
This summer, it was reported that HBO has

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:10.840
released a casting call for George RR Martin's
favorite Targaryen, Daemon Targaryen, key

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.049
figure from this time period of the Dance
of the Dragons.

00:01:14.049 --> 00:01:19.610
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.750
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:26.870
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:32.220
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.200
I's throne.
Both of them thought they belonged on the

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.580
Iron Throne. When people started declaring
for one of them or the other, their fight

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:45.280
divided the kingdoms in two. Targaryens fought
Targaryens, bothers fought brothers, dragons

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.200
fought dragons. By the time it was over, thousands
were dead. The conflict would prove to be

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.880
incredibly destructive for not only House
Targaryen, but large parts of Westeros as

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.229
well. In addition, it devastated the Targaryen's
dragon population, ultimately leading to their

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:04.220
extinction within a few decades.
They never truly recovered.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:08.691
By the end of the reign of King Viserys I
Targaryen, twenty dragons were alive. The

00:02:08.691 --> 00:02:14.330
majority of these died during the civil war
called the Dance of the Dragons, which began

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:20.370
in 129 AC and lasted until mid 131 AC.
One of the main characters in this series

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:24.690
is going to be Daemon Targaryen.
Daemon Targaryen also known as Prince of the

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:29.370
City, Lord Flea Bottom and the Rogue Prince
had many titles throughout his life: Prince,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:34.751
Ser, Commander of the City Watch, Master of
Coin, master of laws, King of the stepstones

00:02:34.751 --> 00:02:39.990
and the narrow sea, protector of the realm.
Daemon was the most controversial man of his

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:45.459
lifetime, an audacious rogue prince and adventurer
who seemed made of good and evil in equal

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:48.050
measure.
There was never a man so loved and so reviled,

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:52.910
and at a same time, as he was.
During the Dance of the Dragons, as the husband

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:58.310
of his niece Rhaenyra, he supported his wife's
claim, and he was considered by many the most

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.489
dangerous man in Westeros.
He was Rhaenyra's second husband, following

00:03:02.489 --> 00:03:06.030
Ser Laenor Velaryon and she was his third
wife.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:10.310
Prince Daemon was the most experienced warrior
of his time and wielded the Valyrian steel

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:15.599
blade Dark Sister. A dragon rider whose dragon
was Caraxes, Daemon declared himself the King

00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:20.030
of the Stepstones and the Narrow Sea.
Daemon was a skilled warrior, described in

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:25.800
the histories as dashing, daring, and dangerous.
He was also ambitious, impetuous, mercurial,

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:31.040
amoral, reckless, and quick to take offense.
He is described as being as charming as he

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.750
was hot-tempered.
And it seems that HBO already found a perfect

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:40.280
fit for the character - Travis Fimmel whom
you might know as Ragnar from Vikings.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.319
It's not yet confirmed that he will play the
role 100%

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:45.940
but it's reported by Portuguese entertainment
website

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:49.760
that he's in talks with HBO to play the role
of Daemon.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.120
Daemon is a versatile character who constantly
switches between being charming and loving

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.390
to crazy and bloodthirsty, and I have to stand
by HBO's side here

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:02.550
as in my opinion Travis Fimmel would be a
great choice to play this George RR Martin's

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.760
favorite character from this time period.
Daemon inspired loyalty.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:12.780
In 106 AC, Daemon led an army to invade the
Stepstones in the southern narrow sea, with

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:18.440
the support of Lord Corlys Velaryon and his
fleet, and with the use of Daemon's dragon,

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.769
Caraxes.
After conquering all but two of the islands,

00:04:21.769 --> 00:04:27.330
Daemon declared himself King of the Stepstones
and the Narrow Sea in 109 AC, being crowned

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:32.320
by Corlys the Sea Snake.
By the year 120 AC Daemon married two times

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:39.120
and had 2 daughters, but both his wives died.
In 120 AC Daemon married again, this time

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.370
to his niece, Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen.
This marriage was performed suddenly without

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:50.080
the knowledge of King Viserys I Targaryen
and was scandalous since neither Laena nor

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:54.590
Laenor Velaryon, Daemon's previous wife, and
Rhaenyra's previous husband, had been dead

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:59.840
for six months. According to Mushroom, it
was Daemon who arranged the death of Laenor

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:05.080
by paying Ser Correy to kill him, thus making
Rhaenyra available to marry.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:11.240
Daemon and Rhaenyra had two sons together,
Prince Aegon the Younger born in 120 AC, and

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:17.380
Prince Viserys, born in 122 AC.
While Viserys I Targaryen had decreed Rhaenyra

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:24.180
Targaryen his heir, Ser Criston Cole crowned
Queen Alicent Hightower's son, Aegon II Targaryen,

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:29.910
after Viserys's death in 129 AC.
The Greens took advantage of being in Kings

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:34.960
Landing at the time of the death of King Viserys
and took the throne while most of the Blacks

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.460
were at Dragonstone.
At the start of the civil war called the Dance

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:44.639
of the Dragons, Prince Daemon had more experience
in warfare than all their foes combined. During

00:05:44.639 --> 00:05:49.020
Rhaenyra's rival coronation on Dragonstone,
Daemon placed the crown of King Jaehaerys

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:55.340
I Targaryen on the head of his wife, proclaiming
her queen and claiming himself Protector of

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:58.930
the Realm.
Daemon led the assault on Harrenhal, capturing

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:04.009
the ruined castle from its castellan.
After hearing of the death of his stepson,

00:06:04.009 --> 00:06:08.580
Prince Lucerys Velaryon, at the hands of his
nephew, Prince Aemond Targaryen,

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:14.509
Daemon, through his spymaster and former mistress
Mysaria, hired Blood and Cheese to murder

00:06:14.509 --> 00:06:20.270
a son of Aegon II. Son for a son.
Daemon abandoned Harrenhal when Aemond and

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:24.380
Criston began marching on the great castle
with a host of greens

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:30.110
Instead, Daemon flew Caraxes back to King's
Landing and assisted Rhaenyra with capturing

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.350
the city.
He made his niece and wife, Rhaenyra the Queen

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:37.930
of the Seven Kingdoms.
Daemon challenged Aemond, waiting for thirteen

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:43.380
days at Harrenhal until Aemond stopped burning
the Riverlands to come face him.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.940
On the 14th day, epic battle above the Gods
Eye finally happened.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.509
It was an aerial duel that took place in the
skies above Harrenhal

00:06:51.509 --> 00:06:57.210
and the Gods Eye between two of the most powerful
living dragons, Vhagar and Caraxes,

00:06:57.210 --> 00:07:00.990
and their riders, Prince Aemond and Prince
Daemon Targaryen.

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:06.539
The duel was said to be a sight to see. The
sun was setting as the two dragons took to

00:07:06.539 --> 00:07:09.850
the sky.
So bright was the Dragonfire that smallfolk

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:14.370
feared the sky was aflame.
When Caraxes attacked Vhagar, she ripped upon

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:19.289
his stomach and tore one of his wings, but
then Caraxes fastened his jaws around her

00:07:19.289 --> 00:07:24.639
throat in a death grip.
These injuries forced them both to cease flying

00:07:24.639 --> 00:07:29.210
and as they tumbled to the water below, Daemon
dueled Aemond to the death.

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:34.810
As he never fastened his saddle, Daemon stood
up on Caraxes and leapt at Aemond, whereupon

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:39.960
he drove his Dark Sister through Aemond's
eye and through his neck, just a second before

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.270
hitting the water.
The Battle Above the Gods Eye ended in the

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:49.669
deaths of both riders and both dragons. Daemon
was forty-nine when he died. Unlike Aemond's

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:54.840
body, however, Daemon's was never found. Singers
say that Daemon lived to spend the rest of

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:59.550
his days in secret with Nettles, but most
historians disagree.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:03.411
If you'd like to know all details about the
upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series, make

00:08:03.411 --> 00:08:07.210
sure to watch my video named ''Game of Thrones
prequel show explained''

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:10.729
in which I as the title says itself - explain
everything about it,

00:08:10.729 --> 00:08:14.460
as well as why reading the book Fire And Blood
does not mean you will know exactly what will

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:18.259
happen on the show.
The books are history of House Targaryen written

00:08:18.259 --> 00:08:21.940
by a Maester
who relies on questionable sources that often

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:26.630
differ from one another
and even George RR Martin said that its accuracy

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:30.090
is not the best.
Once again, let me remind you that: Fire &amp; Blood

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:35.229
is a complete history of House Targaryen
written by George R. R. Martin from a perspective

00:08:35.229 --> 00:08:38.940
of Archmaester Gyldayn
who wrote it many decades after the events

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:42.699
took place.
The show, unlike the book, will contain truth,

00:08:42.699 --> 00:08:47.810
it will depict what actually happened, not
the changed history, fake or semi-true, not

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:51.389
what might or might not have happened.
We will know exactly what happened in this

00:08:51.389 --> 00:08:56.009
time period when the show comes out, and that's
why you cannot just read Fire And Blood book

00:08:56.009 --> 00:08:59.899
and think you would know what actually happen
or what will happen on the show.

00:08:59.899 --> 00:09:03.190
Daemon Targaryen will be one of the main characters
and probably my favorite, just like he is

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.690
George RR Martin's favorite.
In Fire And Blood, Gyldayn uses these words

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:09.410
to best describe Daemon:
''Over the centuries, House Targaryen has

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:15.079
produced both great men and monsters. Prince
Daemon was both. In his day there was not

00:09:15.079 --> 00:09:21.259
a man so admired, so beloved, and so reviled
in all Westeros. He was made of light and

00:09:21.259 --> 00:09:26.579
darkness in equal parts. To some, he was a
hero, to others the blackest of villains.''.

00:09:26.579 --> 00:09:30.689
This is a good description of Daemon.
The best description comes from George RR

00:09:30.689 --> 00:10:23.079
Martin 

00:10:23.079 --> 00:10:24.320
of course:

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:31.610
Anyways, if you want more details about the
prequel, make sure to check out that video.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.759
Let me know your thoughts about everything:
the prequel, its characters,

00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:39.839
especially Daemon and about Travis Fimmel
being in talks with HBO to play it, in the

00:10:39.839 --> 00:10:44.489
comment section down below. Thank you so much
for watching and hope to see you in the next

00:10:44.489 --> 00:10:49.889
one. Peace!

